    "body": "Ready for a re-check. Head 137fbb13e closes the second pre-review.\n- The attention test now drives `fold_chip` and reads the painted shapes. At each height where the title fits, it finds a state text or the warn bar under the title. It uses two state texts and meets the full, glyph and bar cases. A clean chip paints no warn bar.\n- The exact-text tests pin a literal count of 89 warnings. The never-generated test is an exact match.\n- The decision file now says that the light theme warn ink is below 3:1 until #4485 adds `status_warn`. It also says that a pane too short for the title shows only the folded mark.\n- The long doc line in `fold_state.rs` is wrapped.\nQuick gate and clippy are green on this head, with the parent branch as base. The PR stays a draft.\n",
